WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.307
By the end of this module, you should be able to create standard views,

00:00:04.307 --> 00:00:09.332
inspect their definitions and dependencies, explain when a view is updatable,

00:00:09.332 --> 00:00:13.447
and use a check option to control writes through a filtered view.

00:00:13.447 --> 00:00:21.777
You should also understand materialized-view freshness and be able to decide whether logic belongs in a

00:00:21.777 --> 00:00:26.562
statement-level CTE, a reusable standard view, or a stored materialized result.

00:00:26.562 --> 00:00:30.652
Keep a real project in mind as we work through this section—for example,

00:00:30.652 --> 00:00:36.257
a governance project limiting which columns different users can access.

00:00:36.257 --> 00:00:41.852
The technical feature matters because it changes what questions we can answer reliably and how easily another

00:00:41.852 --> 00:00:45.492
analyst can understand our work.

00:00:45.492 --> 00:00:52.507
As you listen, try to connect each SQL or data concept to a decision you might need to

00:00:52.507 --> 00:00:56.062
defend later: what the data means, what one row represents, what can be missing,

00:00:56.062 --> 00:01:00.320
and what assumptions the transformation introduces.
